lines=['# Triple normal lightcurve pipeline: implementation and matched timing','', 'Native static single-source triples with uniform/linear LD now use the ordinary default LightCurve API. No backend flag is supplied in the measurements. Point/hex/integral selection and actual lazy caustic-tree construction are included. Values and tangents share scalar routing, roots and support preparation. Detailed design and scope: IMPLEMENTATION.md; public documentation: docs/python/triple-algebraic.md.','', '## Validation','', '```json',json.dumps(summary['checks'],indent=2),'```', '', 'The Python regressions check all ten LightCurve parameter tangents on point/hex/integral routes, two step sizes where applicable, both coordinate conventions, a secondary-dominant mass case, zero radius, implicit/explicit backend equivalence and three captured scalar-error failures. The binary ordinary-call regression subset remains unchanged. No runtime derivative-error contract is introduced. The six earlier lens configurations were extended to seven, with two radii, U/LD and relative1e-3/1e-4. VBM SinglePoly and MultiPoly reference values use relative1e-7/absolute0. All raw values, flags, routes and differences are retained in matrix.json. Agreement is evidence for this matrix, not a universal precision certificate.']
